      },
      "before": "| operation (`analyze`, `install`, `remove`, `update-index`, trust refresh) | open-then-verify of every executed or loaded closure member on its opened fd (the core itself and the component binaries about to run), not an eager hash of the whole inventory | decision evaluation with write-ahead `evalHighWater` (\u00a74.2) | yes, under \u00a75.6 | \u2014 |",
      "after": "| operation (`analyze`, `install`, `remove`, `update-index`, trust refresh) | open-then-verify of every executed or loaded closure member on its opened fd (the core itself and the component binaries about to run), not an eager hash of the whole inventory | decision evaluation with write-ahead `evalHighWater` (\u00a74.2) | yes, under \u00a75.6 | \u2014 |\n\nThe creator-only pre-installation sequence in docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md is an explicit exception to dependence on a pre-existing I/fence/current capsule: it authenticates original account/core/profile/embedded provenance before effects and publishes unbootstrapped P0 with unevaluated clock. It grants no ordinary role standing, time admission or requested analysis permission; those still require ordinary admission afterwards."
    },
    {
      "parent": {
        "path": "docs/coop/completion/security-completion.v8.md",
        "bytes": 69988,
        "sha256": "54f3a6901d4192c5b6af82d4aad4414a84ee3b7748aa67cae06272a481e38c2d"
      },
      "selector": {
        "line": 322
      },
      "before": "journal append, quarantine marker, SC-TRUST high-water copy, lifecycle publication, selection commit.",
      "after": "journal append, quarantine marker, SC-TRUST high-water copy, lifecycle publication, selection commit. Additional initial-root boundaries are H confirmation; each fixed/staged directory and containing parent; final exclusive-rename I-parent confirmation; and existing-root I-directory/I-parent confirmation for writes. Their exact ordering, original observations and one act-wide budget are owned by docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md. Metadata/doctor/observation-only surfaces gain no barrier permission. Existing selected primitive and typed uncertainty rules remain."
    },
    {
      "parent": {
        "path": "docs/implementation/m1/source-selection-v2/reference/effective-workflows-and-surfaces.md",
        "bytes": 139497,
        "sha256": "4478ce1a69369cd0b430fd5d3fc695e8372219629b05a08ae6642a845cab794d"
      },
      "selector": {
        "line": 1300
      },
      "before": "`doctor.defectsFound`. Only an unproducible report is `HOST.IO_FAILURE` (4), with detail `DOCTOR.REPORT_NOT_PRODUCIBLE`.",
      "after": "`doctor.defectsFound`. Only an unproducible report is `HOST.IO_FAILURE` (4), with detail `DOCTOR.REPORT_NOT_PRODUCIBLE`. For an observed complete I, the native doctor assembler adds one registered INSTALLATION.DURABILITY_NOT_CHECKED informational detail. Only that code is excluded from numeric defectsFound and DOCTOR.DEFECTS_FOUND selection. Capacity is255 actual defects plus the notice;256 actual defects refuse and latch instead of truncation. The result/count/goldens and current registry must activate together. Trust doctor/store status add no notice/channel. See docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md."
    },
    {
      "parent": {
        "path": "docs/implementation/m2/project-registry-owner-selection-v2/owner.md",
        "bytes": 32488,
        "sha256": "2d4b65c9b0bc088b2667c35e75bf82d1702d13703be6effb1df975e7c67c179f"
      },
      "selector": {
        "line": 9
      },
      "before": "This owner introduces private registry encoding and internal observation kinds only. It adds no public command, wire field, semantic identity input, signature domain, role state or public error code. Existing operation owners must supply authorization for installation, first-write, explicit recovery, move, fork, adoption and retirement. Their absence is not permission to invent a CLI surface or initialize on an ordinary read.",
      "after": "This owner introduces private registry encoding and internal observation kinds only. It adds no public command, wire field, semantic identity input, signature domain, role state or public error code. Existing operation owners must supply authorization for installation, first-write, explicit recovery, move, fork, adoption and retirement. Their absence is not permission to invent a CLI surface or initialize on an ordinary read. The separately reviewed initial-root-binding owner supplies only initial installation publication and ordinary selected-store binding; its positive creator predicate, fixed-root storage choice, read/write split, bounded original-owner sequence and complete P0 publication are mandatory. Other recovery/move/fork/adoption/retirement owners remain separate. See docs/implementation/m2/initial-root-binding-owner-selection-v1/owner.md."
    },
    {
